cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "GraviLens: A Physics-Informed Vision Transformer for Dark Matter Classification via Strong Gravitational Lensing"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-19
repository-code: "https://github.com/mahoutei/GraviLens-SIS"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  GraviLens is a physics-informed Swin-style vision transformer for
  strong-gravitational-lensing image classification, trained and evaluated
  against five baseline architectures (Lensformer, LensPINN-Small, ViT,
  CaiT, ViTSD) in the v9 benchmark. This repository contains the final
  training, evaluation, and visualization code.
authors:
  - family-names: Catiil
    given-names: "Dean Mark H."
keywords:
  - strong gravitational lensing
  - dark matter
  - physics-informed neural network
  - vision transformer
  - image classification
  - singular isothermal sphere
